#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:209
msgid "Permission and access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:212
msgid "Why can't I see the Access Control tab in Channel Settings?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:214
msgid ""
"The **Access Control** tab is only visible when all of these conditions "
"are met:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:216
msgid "You have Channel Admin role or higher for the channel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:217
msgid ""
"The channel is a private channel (not public, group message, or direct "
"message)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:218
msgid ""
"ABAC is enabled system-wide by a System Admin in **System Console > "
"System Attributes > Attribute-Based Access**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:219
msgid "Your user role includes the ``manage_channel_access_rules`` permission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:222
msgid "Can Channel and Team Admins override system policies?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:224
msgid ""
"No. Channel rules are always **additive** to system policies. Users must "
"satisfy both system policies AND channel rules to access the channel. "
"Channel and Team Admins cannot weaken or override restrictions set by "
"System Admins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:227
msgid "What happens if I create rules that would exclude myself?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:229
msgid ""
"Mattermost prevents this with self-exclusion validation. If your rules "
"would remove you from the channel, you'll see an error message and cannot"
" save the changes until you adjust the rules or reset them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:232
msgid "Rule configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:235
msgid "Can I use advanced CEL expressions in Channel Settings?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:237
msgid ""
"No. Channel Settings only supports Basic Mode with simple attribute "
"conditions. For complex expressions with nested logic or mixed operators,"
" System Admins need to create policies in the System Console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:240
msgid "How do I remove all access rules from a channel?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:242
msgid ""
"Delete all attribute conditions from the access rules table. When no "
"rules are configured and no system policies are applied, the channel "
"returns to standard access behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:245
msgid "Why is the auto-sync toggle disabled?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:247
msgid "The auto-sync toggle is automatically disabled when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:249
msgid "No access rules are configured"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:250
msgid ""
"A system policy with auto-sync enabled is applied (Channel and Team "
"Admins cannot disable it)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:251
msgid "There are validation errors in the current rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:252
msgid "The channel's access control policy is not in an active state"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:256
msgid ""
"**Troubleshooting auto-sync issues**: If auto-sync functionality "
"(automatic adding/re-adding of members) is not working as expected, "
"verify that the channel's access control policy is in an active state. An"
" inactive policy will prevent automatic member additions from occurring. "
"Note that enforcement of rules (removal of members who no longer meet "
"requirements) happens regardless of the policy's active state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:259
msgid "Synchronization and membership"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:262
msgid "How quickly are membership changes applied?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:264
msgid ""
"When you save access rules, membership sync job is created and changes "
"are applied as soon as the job is completed. Additionally, Mattermost "
"runs synchronization jobs every 30 minutes to handle attribute changes "
"from external systems (LDAP, SAML)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:267
msgid "Will users be notified when they're removed from a channel?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:269
msgid ""
"Yes, users receive standard Mattermost notifications when they're removed"
" from channels due to access rule changes, similar to manual removals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:272
msgid "Can I see who was added or removed during synchronization?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:274
msgid ""
"Yes, the confirmation modal before saving shows exactly which users will "
"be affected. System Admins can also view detailed synchronization logs in"
" the System Console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:277
msgid "Attribute and data questions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:280
msgid "Which user attributes can I use in access rules?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:282
msgid ""
"You can use any user attributes either synchronized via LDAP/SAML or "
"manually configured by System Admins in **System Console > System "
"Attributes > User Attributes**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:285
msgid "What happens if a user attribute changes?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:287
msgid ""
"During the next synchronization (every 30 minutes), users who no longer "
"match the access rules will be removed from the channel, and new users "
"who now match will be added (if auto-sync is enabled)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:290
msgid "Do guest users work with ABAC channels?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:292
msgid ""
"No. Private channels with attribute-based access control cannot have "
"guest users. This ensures strict adherence to access control policies "
"based on organizational attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:295
msgid "Can group-sync channels use ABAC?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/abac-channel-access-rules.rst:297
msgid ""
"No. Channels configured with group synchronization cannot use attribute-"
"based access control. Group-sync and ABAC are mutually exclusive features"
" - you must choose one method of access control per channel."
msgstr ""

